    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλεος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Att.
		 masc. and neut. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλεως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span>, but fem. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπλέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					83d
				</span></i>
			:—pl., nom. masc. and fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλεῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					196e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				98.8
			</span></i>, neut. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>de An.</u>
					423a27
				</span></i>
			: acc. masc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					516e
				</span></i>
			:—<i>quite full of</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτερῶν λέγουσι ἀνάπλεον εἶναι τὸν
					ἠέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ψιμυθίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					1072
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
			</span></i> l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότους ἀ. οἱ ὀφθαλμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					516e
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>infected,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ σώματος ἀναπλέα [ἡ ψυχή</span>]
				<i>with</i> the body, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				83d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτὸ τὸ καλὸν μὴ ἀ. σαρκῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					211e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐσμεν τοῦ μὴ καθαρῶς διαλέγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					196e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
